{"id":"rephaim-or-giants","name":"Rephaim, Or Giants, The","aliases":["Rephaim"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:rephaim-or-giants-the"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Rephaim","text":"Lofty men; giants, (Gen. 14:5; 2 Sam. 21:16, 18, marg. A.V., Rapha, marg. R.V., Raphah; Deut. 3:13, R.V.; A.V., “giants”). The aborigines of Palestine, afterwards conquered and dispossessed by the Canaanite tribes, are classed under this general title. They were known to the Moabites as Emim, i.e., “fearful”, (Deut. 2:11), and to the Ammonites as Zamzummim. Some of them found refuge among the Philistines, and were still existing in the days of David. We know nothing of their origin. They were not necessarily connected with the “giants” (R.V., “Nephilim”) of Gen. 6:4. (See GIANTS.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7497","lemma":"רָפָא","xlit":"râphâʼ","gloss":"a giant","kjv":"giant, Rapha, Rephaim. See also H1051","count":10,"share":0.56},{"strong":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","xlit":"Pᵉlishtîy","gloss":"a Pelishtite or inhabitant of Pelesheth","kjv":"Philistine","count":9,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H4421","lemma":"מִלְחָמָה","xlit":"milchâmâh","gloss":"a battle","kjv":"battle, fight, war","count":5,"share":0.28},{"strong":"H1661","lemma":"גַּת","xlit":"Gath","gloss":"Gath, a Philistine city","kjv":"Gath","count":3,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H1359","lemma":"גֹּב","xlit":"Gôb","gloss":"Gob, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Gob","count":2,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H6010","lemma":"עֵמֶק","xlit":"ʻêmeq","gloss":"a vale","kjv":"dale, vale, valley . See also H1025","count":3,"share":0.17}],"verses":["Gen.14.5","Josh.13.12","Josh.15.8","Josh.17.15","2Sam.5.18","2Sam.21.16","2Sam.21.18","2Sam.21.20","2Sam.21.22","Isa.17.5","1Sam.17.4","1Sam.17.49","1Sam.17.50","2Sam.5.25","2Sam.21.15","2Sam.21.17","2Sam.21.19","2Sam.21.21"],"related":[{"id":"goliath","type":"cooccur","shared":8,"jaccard":0.308,"why":"8 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"rephaim","type":"cooccur","shared